Prompt:

Theme: {fashion / sport / music / lifestyle / etc.}
Brand / Event: {name}
Main word: {4–8 letter keyword}
Person: {age, gender, outfit, vibe}
Held object: {bag / helmet / vinyl / bouquet / etc.}
Accent color: {color}
Aspect ratio: 9:16

Create a bold editorial poster combining realistic photography, oversized typography, and connected forced perspective.

The person must physically hold or control the foreground object. Keep one continuous, believable perspective chain:

body → shoulder → arm → wrist → hand → grip point → object.

The same object being held should extend naturally toward the camera and appear oversized only because it is very close to the lens. Do not place a separate oversized object in the foreground.

Use a low-angle wide-lens perspective with the person slightly farther back and the hand/object closest to camera. Keep the grip, fingers, arm, and object physically connected and anatomically correct.

Place a huge condensed sans-serif keyword behind the person, partially covered by the body, arm, and object to create real depth.

Add small editorial information around the edges using meaningful brand, event, product, date, location, or specification details.

Use a warm off-white paper background, subtle print grain, mostly black typography, and one restrained accent color.

Keep the composition clean, fashion-forward, realistic, and dimensional.

